Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Fix findings of the fresh-copy verification of the final
 package

Assets: the _reproduction_cpu head records reproduction_distilbert_first_token, which no
archive contained, so its documented evaluate / end-to-end commands failed. The cache archive
is rebuilt as Feature_Caches_merged_20261018_v2.zip with that cache added (tensors
byte-identical to distilbert_first_token). Run_Outputs_20261018_v2.zip drops the meme review
grid (it is in Git) and shortens machine-specific path prefixes in its step logs. The
diagnostic checkpoint archive gets its own README. docs/Multimodal_Assets.md lists the four
_v2 archives with sizes and SHA-256 and maps every earlier archive to its replacement.

Docs: say where the archives live and that a public repository must not carry the review
evidence; scope the regeneration claim to the multimodal files; correct the TF32 emulation
bound (>= 0.9999999), the overfitting caveat (which heads reach train AUC 0.999), the
selection-optimism note, two notebook claims, the known-problems list, and the fast-route
output folder; note that the two 20261001 image heads have no run folder; mark image-group
branch and commit references as history of the original team repository; explain the
"team README x.y" citations; fill in the directory guide.

Code and packaging: end_to_end.py and check_tf32_emulation.py record local encoder copies
by folder name instead of an absolute path (the three committed reports are updated the
same way); train.sh / trainer.py examples pass the shipped image cache; pydantic>=2 is a
listed serving dependency; .gitattributes keeps *.sh and the Dockerfile LF; .dockerignore
covers nested archives, checkpoints and logs; the checkpoint manifest uses LF.

